  "ragExplanation": "AI Search uses RAG (retrieval-augmented generation). It does not answer from the AI's memory.\n\n1. The AI turns your question into Pāḷi search terms.\n2. TPR searches the Tipiṭaka on your device with them.\n3. The AI reads the passages found, keeps the ones that answer your question, and sums them up.\n\nEvery result is a real passage you can open and check.\n\nAn AI chat answers from what it remembers. It can sound certain and still be wrong, and it seldom shows where an answer comes from. Use AI Search to find the passages, and read them to know what the texts say.",
